1. Definitions

Theme means the Synth Astro theme package, including its source code,
components, layouts, styles, configuration, documentation, and included demo
content.

End Product means a customized website, publication, or application created
using the Theme.

Licensee means the person, business, or organization that purchased a valid
license.

Client means a third party for whom the Licensee creates an End Product.

2. License Grant

After purchasing a valid license, you may use the Theme to create an unlimited
number of End Products for yourself or for your clients.

Each End Product may be a commercial website, publication, or application.

You may:

- install, edit, and customize the Theme;
- modify source code, styles, components, content, and configuration;
- deploy customized End Products to production;
- create local backups and private version-control copies for your licensed
  projects;
- use the Theme for an unlimited number of personal, commercial, or client
  projects;
- hand off customized End Products to your clients;
- access lifetime updates for the Theme, as described in this license.

3. Client Handoff

You may hand off an End Product to a Client, including the customized source
code needed to maintain that specific End Product.

The Client may use, edit, and maintain that End Product.

The Client may not extract, reuse, redistribute, resell, sublicense, share, or
repurpose the original Theme as a template, starter kit, boilerplate, source
package, UI kit, or competing product.

4. Lifetime Updates

A valid license includes lifetime access to updates for the Theme.

Lifetime updates may include bug fixes, compatibility updates, improvements,
new components, design refinements, documentation updates, and other changes
released by the author for the same Theme.

"Lifetime" means the lifetime of the Theme as a maintained product. XOCO WEB
SRL may stop maintaining, updating, selling, or distributing the Theme at its
discretion.

Lifetime updates do not include custom development, custom support,
installation services, migration services, or work made specifically for an
individual Licensee or Client unless agreed separately in writing.

